<title>POLAND: STALEXPORT WINS $5.6 MLN CONTRACTS.</title>
<headline>STALEXPORT WINS $5.6 MLN CONTRACTS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish steel trader Stalexport SA has signed several contracts worth a total of $5.6 million for the export of several tens of thousands of tonnes of steel to the Near East, Argentina and Egypt, Stalexport said.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement on Tuesday that the contract, supplying steel from the Huta Katowice mill, was seen carried out at the turn of the first and second quarters this year. </p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
